cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you reference the PointSav Factory Release Engineering governance
  repository, please cite using these metadata.
type: software
title: "Factory Release Engineering — PointSav Digital Systems"
abstract: >-
  PointSav Digital Systems' release engineering and governance repository.
  Canonical source for licensing matrices (LICENSE-MATRIX.md), contributor
  licence agreements, trademark policy, compliance playbook, and
  per-repository publication rules for the pointsav/* and woodfine/* GitHub
  organisations. Implements Stage 5 of the vendor → customer → deployments
  commit flow defined by PointSav release-engineering governance (vendor → customer → deployments).
authors:
  - name: "PointSav Digital Systems"
    email: open.source@pointsav.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/pointsav/factory-release-engineering"
url: "https://github.com/pointsav/factory-release-engineering"
# No single SPDX identifier applies — this repo is MIXED (per-directory:
# licenses/ upstream copyright, policies|headers|mapping CC-BY-4.0, scripts
# AGPL-3.0-or-later, cla all-rights-reserved; see NEXT.md DEF-005). Corrected
# 2026-08-02 — was LicenseRef-PointSav-ARR, contradicting this repo's own
# MIXED classification in LICENSE-MATRIX.md §3.1 and repo-license-map.yaml.
license-url: "https://github.com/pointsav/factory-release-engineering/blob/main/LICENSE-MATRIX.md"
version: "0.1.132"
date-released: "2026-05-12"
keywords:
  - release-engineering
  - governance
  - licensing
  - contributor-license-agreement
  - trademark
  - compliance
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: "https://github.com/pointsav/factory-release-engineering/blob/main/LICENSE-MATRIX.md"
    description: Repository licence matrix — all pointsav/* and woodfine/* repos
